You are completely correct. In your frontend code, you are currently using the external API endpoint (/JE/voucher-transactions/search-vid), but you already have your own internal API (/JS/voucher/active) ready to go. We just need to add the LISTAGG join for the Issue Categories to your backend so the frontend can render those Chips correctly!
Here are the exact changes for the Backend and Frontend to switch to your own robust API.
### 1. Backend Change (VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java)
Find the getAvailableVouchersVid method (around line 1160) and replace the SQL query with this updated version that fetches the comma-separated issue categories:
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getAvailableVouchersVid(Long roleId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                rv.ID,
                rv.VID,
                rv.DESCRIPTION,
                c.CATEGORY_NAME,
                
                -- NEW: Fetch and comma-separate all mapped Issue Categories
                (
                    SELECT LISTAGG(ic.ISSUE_CATEGORY_NAME, ', ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY ic.ISSUE_CATEGORY_NAME)
                    FROM REQUEST_VOUCHER_ISSUE_CATEGORY rvic
                    JOIN ISSUE_CATEGORY ic ON rvic.ISSUE_CATEGORY_ID = ic.ID
                    WHERE rvic.REQUEST_VOUCHER_ID = rv.ID
                ) AS ISSUE_CATEGORIES,

                rv.CREATED_BY AS CREATOR_ID,
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, rv.CREATED_BY) AS CREATOR_NAME,
                rv.CREATED_AT
            FROM REQUEST_VOUCHER rv
            LEFT JOIN VOUCHER_CATEGORY c ON rv.CATEGORY_ID = c.ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON rv.CREATED_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE rv.ALLOWED_ROLE = ? AND rv.STATUS = 'ACTIVE'
            ORDER BY rv.CREATED_AT DESC
        """;

       return jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, roleId);
    }

```
